# It is the reference for the record numbering of EMV 4.3 Book 1 section
# 12.3.2: the terminal reads the directory from the record 1 and stops when the
# card answers '6A83'. The card is a UnionPay IC card certification test card,
# its records carry the label "for test use only".
#
# Select PSE, the directory is in the SFI 1
send: 00 A4 04 00 0E 31 50 41 59 2E 53 59 53 2E 44 44 46 30 31 00
resp: 6F 15 84 0E 31 50 41 59 2E 53 59 53 2E 44 44 46 30 31 A5 03 88 01 01 90 00
# Record 1
send: 00 B2 01 0C 00
resp: 70 1C 61 1A 4F 08 A0 00 00 03 33 01 01 02 50 0B 55 49 43 43 20 43 52 45 44 49 54 87 01 01 90 00
# Record 2
send: 00 B2 02 0C 00
resp: 70 1B 61 19 4F 08 A0 00 00 03 33 01 01 01 50 0A 55 49 43 43 20 44 45 42 49 54 87 01 02 90 00
# Record 3
send: 00 B2 03 0C 00
resp: 70 21 61 1F 4F 08 A0 00 00 03 33 01 01 03 50 10 55 49 43 43 20 51 55 41 53 49 43 52 45 44 49 54 87 01 03 90 00
# Record 4 does not exist, the directory ends here
send: 00 B2 04 0C 00
resp: 6A 83
